#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064219 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064091 :question/id #uuid "3e89a278-54ab-59a6-adb6-38f43c0fbe9a" :question/math-academy-id "e-471" :question/problem "Calculate the integral  $$\n\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int \\dfrac{3}{2(1 + 25x^2)} = \\dfrac 3 2 \\int \\dfrac{1}{1+25x^2}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^2}\\textrm{d}u =\\arctan u +C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $25x^2 = (5x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 5\\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2+50{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡5x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "227abe29-6e31-5afd-b0ca-3b8ed7d8c287" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691123 :question-generator/id #uuid "db292685-492c-577a-a81a-e28054437854" :question-generator/script "generators/e7/e7ec9a4376033301e7fc3bf5e04dfb06f0c0a280a6d353170d03a3339441ced4/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b3f469d-d785-54c0-8500-e4f4c541c311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330478} {:answer/id #uuid "44fe7e54-fa6e-59d5-8a26-f4f36bb5501f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330572} {:answer/id #uuid "848d8e79-5f9b-50c9-a7a2-c023a98ccebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331128} {:answer/id #uuid "be85cd80-7bd6-5b67-8980-2e785a3889ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331634} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4584df-c775-5f4a-a59c-6d2f35a59525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be85cd80-7bd6-5b67-8980-2e785a3889ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331634} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e5cefbe-1794-5312-8f1f-f28eb36bbc55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332307}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ff7c3e1-6732-5fb3-bcd2-7ed1aeab0712" :question/math-academy-id "q-49540" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{6}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo. let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(3x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0edb1c73-87ee-58c2-a730-43e7f693d596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330078} {:answer/id #uuid "26074d64-e780-5986-be16-fa82ceeb0164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330281} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec2d31d-3894-565f-9b91-3bc180c6d541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330506} {:answer/id #uuid "581c2751-ecf3-5021-a41f-a828e408e3cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330735} {:answer/id #uuid "59dbc6dd-87a6-5e93-99fe-8c88f23299aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec2d31d-3894-565f-9b91-3bc180c6d541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330506} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef0aa3c5-1f7e-5feb-b2ae-0f439aa2181d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332622}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea76ea1f-1600-5c9d-b198-b9fb197580ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-49548" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{9\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/9)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b46bc9-97cb-5bce-918b-8b92646973b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247570} {:answer/id #uuid "1b1e75f2-49eb-5a5d-9cee-c6ed60930c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247668} {:answer/id #uuid "3de5bd43-5bd8-5d01-8064-06ac8fdb185f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{