answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "483c26c4-9591-5693-b37b-d4073beefda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248071} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8b07a0-116b-518d-9a1d-972a85844f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249098} {:answer/id #uuid "c32179fe-c467-592c-9f69-b60802a05b4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249159} {:answer/id #uuid "d304c17e-5ea8-5a66-93d7-6a99599f2090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249297} {:answer/id #uuid "fd94393a-c5bd-52f0-be8f-368ed42e2eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d304c17e-5ea8-5a66-93d7-6a99599f2090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249297} :answer-field/id #uuid "204c0449-cb8b-5901-a89b-496c8ed2dd4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249729}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9cca3e1-79d8-525d-a321-dda6d6f0fe18" :question/math-academy-id "q-114045" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{8}{16+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{16+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{16\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/16)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/16}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{16+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245b618d-7b28-597c-b19b-5c843eb6c7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247741} {:answer/id #uuid "52fe1c8c-100b-5622-9e05-9387df536621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(9x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248173} {:answer/id #uuid "a0850bb9-1690-5ca5-b8a2-6fbde9a42a7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248858} {:answer/id #uuid "b7508ec8-5378-54d4-bd32-a71a1b47afaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249065} {:answer/id #uuid "bbaf321e-a0ba-506b-a6c1-81f09db011a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7508ec8-5378-54d4-bd32-a71a1b47afaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249065} :answer-field/id #uuid "835d8e84-7024-5e35-bbe8-a87537867361" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249899}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e7b39f3-407b-599d-a487-d698e967777b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114046" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{9}{81\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/81)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/81}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/9)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\n The only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{9}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{9}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=9\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/9)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (9\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "486b0a70-7e05-52ff-8487-81ba071e0a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288533} {:answer/id #uuid "69127801-3533-5a03-b74d-9ec2a87d6eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288771} {:answer/id #uuid "e96eb19b-978a-5ee7-bb01-e9ab119611d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(16x)}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289582} {:answer/id #uuid "ef828203-a491-5804-b360-380890b2c51b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289611} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a54489-77bd-54ff-ae37-733d7622bf54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(8x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "486b0a70-7e05-52ff-8487-81ba071e0a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288533} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ebda31b-7ff5-5da1-8d90-6d8cb199795a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289933}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3817a61-9f5a-501b-a646-24bc46868497" :question/math-academy-id "q-2504" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $16{x}^{2}=(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(4x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15325872-4e2f-544f-9dec-000683e3691e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288177} {:answer/id #uuid "164243e9-717c-580d-9d74-331ac357f68c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288180} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7d4913-276e-5926-8683-f107a4d1158c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(25x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288790} {:answer/id #uuid "87403b08-b913-5b5b-af1b-47f906da3828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288944} {:answer/id #uuid "90b08433-72df-5a70-8a55-aec7b22f8981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(25x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "164243e9-717c-580d-9d74-331ac357f68c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288180} :answer-field/id #uuid "589b96c3-feba-5f82-b690-a05fef9d4fc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289916}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d025ad08-0459-5553-af22-02ed776a0b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-2507" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $25{x}^{2}=(5x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024f569b-84cc-57ef-8f4d-9dc8de0df792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329984} {:answer/id #uuid "12e1d549-32b5-52ba-8653-965154243838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330111} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd86b9e-f501-52cd-b1cc-9ff1facc3fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330482} {:answer/id #uuid "6428015d-361f-5b50-9364-a1602259dd12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330841} {:answer/id #uuid "fbaac824-d193-5f69-9c43-16185bc76ba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "024f569b-84cc-57ef-8f4d-9dc8de0df792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329984} :answer-field/id #uuid "21cb126f-fb81-5a2d-8f46-32591eb308f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332250}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00f3edb2-19bb-54fa-b405-1ba68902442b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49505" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{4+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{4+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{4\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)}^{2}.$ \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{4+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22bf65d9-1368-5c83-bc06-2f787ae31aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330249} {:answer/id #uuid "b84605c3-6d64-59e4-a03f-63d799bb1439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331577} {:answer/id #uuid "c163d792-fcdb-58ce-be5c-05660a506b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331666} {:answer/id #uuid "c187c878-5877-5b0a-ab41-952209abe59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331668} {:answer/id #uuid "e20ac18c-ab7a-518f-8d37-1b59b1612d09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22bf65d9-1368-5c83-bc06-2f787ae31aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330249} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6a8623-72fb-5f8a-9e38-396d560f8321" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332330}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73d1e60d-39c3-527b-ad50-26d30b66cdba" :question/math-academy-id "q-49550" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{25\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/25)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/25}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{25+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0218ebee-f46b-52a3-af27-002bd2e16fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{8}\\right)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329977} {:answer/id #uuid "2d0a098d-fa78-5f98-bfe7-2e76cd1fe7ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330349} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1c856a-d31e-5281-a2a6-f20cbee86a40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(8x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330499} {:answer/id #uuid "6da04d85-0964-58d1-bd80-e9e62694fa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{8}\\right)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330930} {:answer/id #uuid "e57ddc07-4a02-59ea-b4b1-dd526c6b3d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{8}\\right)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6da04d85-0964-58d1-bd80-e9e62694fa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{8}\\right)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330930} :answer-field/id #uuid "d448c3a1-6bd6-56fc-a1f7-e15ec5601f57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332573}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e79ee700-e1a2-5377-9595-991fdfcefa49" :question/math-academy-id "q-49551" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{64+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{64+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{64\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/64)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{64}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/64}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/8)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{8}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{8}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=8\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{64+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/8)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (8\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{8}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26b8753a-d28b-5470-8f73-93050c06c08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339465} {:answer/id #uuid "6b85678e-6139-5d36-af17-0b94102122cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340081} {:answer/id #uuid "a2fa1f1a-bb6b-520e-bae1-d824104a01c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340605} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8d3b36-56c7-55f4-abd1-ab704350e9ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340693} {:answer/id #uuid "fb91a9c0-e0c4-502a-ae2f-5e69dfe1bc66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b85678e-6139-5d36-af17-0b94102122cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340081} :answer-field/id #uuid "1611e707-c42e-5085-bbf5-4935f8f58d88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341418}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93802a48-b09b-52e0-870e-185ec5edc9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-73714" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{36\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/36)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/36}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=6\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (6\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc0eaaa6-3c74-5955-ab7a-40c09fa2a964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368718} {:answer/id #uuid "6b672eef-fdca-5016-828c-47d6af33c13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368719} {:answer/id #uuid "ce69df23-6261-537f-bc31-f5d9599f5543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368720} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c8552a-dd1c-59c6-825b-7bdb5b09d5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368721} {:answer/id #uuid "250a9a15-df5f-58ee-9c74-d26e624f24b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "250a9a15-df5f-58ee-9c74-d26e624f24b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4164c5-58af-56ae-8f11-f8cd84fa0fda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368717}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6decd4b-7a1d-5fb8-8bf2-963b2f6581d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73713" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{10}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo. let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1+(2x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b31a011-34d6-54fb-97d3-f5fd61f6b537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427995} {:answer/id #uuid "68c27e18-cd86-5136-97ff-930ab97daa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427996} {:answer/id #uuid "74bba607-5459-5096-9775-251242509188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427997} {:answer/id #uuid "bbcb8ff0-bcc8-5c73-8990-398286767616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428001} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2fa96a-ca7c-53d2-b91f-002c52d75021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b31a011-34d6-54fb-97d3-f5fd61f6b537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427995} :answer-field/id #uuid "a430fc00-ecdb-5355-9c79-98aa358084c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "276f25e8-0fe6-5cab-8eeb-f55147c6c339" :question/math-academy-id "q-114039" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{1+6{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $6{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{6}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+6{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676705 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04213b8c-a4f5-5d3a-9b15-2026b2773f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(\\frac{x}{9} \\right)}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676706} {:answer/id #uuid "24ff35a2-12cf-5cee-878e-d0b766426a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{x}{9} \\right)}}{729}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676730} {:answer/id #uuid "2b636129-5f39-51a3-84e5-2abd974c2009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(x \\right)}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676734} {:answer/id #uuid "771066be-5b08-556f-82d9-049a0d3f3ddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{x}{9} \\right)}}{81}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676783} {:answer/id #uuid "d8bc0d3a-5228-5caf-9e16-ef5c59b3a33b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{x}{9} \\right)}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8bc0d3a-5228-5caf-9e16-ef5c59b3a33b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{x}{9} \\right)}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676842} :answer-field/id #uuid "33c84b16-473c-5bf4-9598-3a717f823644" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676746}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0328f6eb-ab94-54f1-a3fa-9db716e7cc30" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8}{x^{2} + 81}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 81=81(1+(\\frac{1}{81})x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{x}{9}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{9},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(9)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{8}{x^{2} + 81}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{8}{81}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\frac{x}{9})^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{8}{81}(9)\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{8}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{8 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}}{9}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{8 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{x}{9} \\right)}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63e93ad6-e0d0-5c38-a11b-a59fd1a7feb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(x \\right)}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676768} {:answer/id #uuid "6915e116-1429-5a3d-90cb-b690b761d7f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(6 x \\right)}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676772} {:answer/id #uuid "8615610f-6718-58b0-a5cc-3146d3e191c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(6 x \\right)}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676791} {:answer/id #uuid "dbce6603-839a-5774-be2a-bd2c88ff96c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(6 x \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676846} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe0f613-0528-5577-bdd1-de1020e9994c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(6 x \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6915e116-1429-5a3d-90cb-b690b761d7f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(6 x \\right)}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676772} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d30795-9bf1-5254-991e-6ab1bff62e9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676806}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "08182b49-5105-5e47-82b6-061be00c1c00" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{252 x^{2} + 7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n252 x^{2} + 7=7(1+(36)x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=6 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=6,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{6})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{4}{252 x^{2} + 7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{7}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(6 x)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{7}(\\frac{1}{6})\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2}{21}\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}}{21}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(6 x \\right)}}{21}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1396f0ef-e9ef-5af5-a333-a4d0c5e73f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(8 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676719} {:answer/id #uuid "1edc6b38-1c31-5835-92d0-b46e9fbae931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(8 x \\right)}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676725} {:answer/id #uuid "8a786436-9219-596e-a6f7-b41b5ab5f943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(x \\right)}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676797} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4e8c8b-124e-5303-bdb6-3adc03547b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(8 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676798} {:answer/id #uuid "be1fd41f-de13-59ad-adea-a77d1673b296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(8 x \\right)}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1edc6b38-1c31-5835-92d0-b46e9fbae931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(8 x \\right)}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676725} :answer-field/id #uuid "bff92d75-29b5-505e-9429-a2ff32acf0cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676825}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29b02aca-6052-5e7a-87ee-eeebee2626d4" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{64 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=8 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=8,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{8})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{3}{64 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 3\\int \\frac{1}{1+(8 x)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 3(\\frac{1}{8})\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{3 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}}{8}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{3 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(8 x \\right)}}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef8c30d-fd49-5779-9e5d-c7dd5a32f59e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7} \\right)}}{343}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676740} {:answer/id #uuid "42157c23-e7cf-53d6-a1f4-7ab4e415c97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7} \\right)}}{49}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676753} {:answer/id #uuid "47b39529-65b9-5548-844f-982292e23a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7} \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676754} {:answer/id #uuid "8696acc0-a3e5-5d84-91ff-758690518877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(x \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676792} {:answer/id #uuid "f2bacbd4-300f-5c95-9a1b-adb46900035f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7} \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2bacbd4-300f-5c95-9a1b-adb46900035f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7} \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676866} :answer-field/id #uuid "89dc5d2d-8f9e-5319-aac2-fdf6c46997c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676796}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2dc8364c-3b6b-5d4f-a269-88d33ebce849" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{2 x^{2} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n2 x^{2} + 49=49(1+(\\frac{2}{49})x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{7},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{7 \\sqrt{2}}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{4}{2 x^{2} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{49}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7})^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{49}(\\frac{7 \\sqrt{2}}{2})\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{7}\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}}{7}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{7} \\right)}}{7}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac2c4b5-4376-5a26-82cd-28b6e5fef581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676765} {:answer/id #uuid "a09fdd28-10ed-5146-a8c9-c78e47e3a98d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676805} {:answer/id #uuid "a7abed00-599b-52be-a273-794e20b361cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676808} {:answer/id #uuid "b0bcc72f-effc-5119-94d9-67b8acd9060a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676816} {:answer/id #uuid "f58d9e97-798b-599a-9014-01605b801daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(x \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0bcc72f-effc-5119-94d9-67b8acd9060a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676816} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4aefbc3-b1af-5b1a-a090-48229e2c59c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676838}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "540dfc73-65b7-5e01-852a-1098e492d974" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{3 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=\\sqrt{3} x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\sqrt{3},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{4}{3 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 4\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\sqrt{3} x)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 4(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d7d4c0f-5fa0-5f80-a5f5-aa0c2d376c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 \\sqrt{5} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5} \\right)}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676715} {:answer/id #uuid "337c7bc0-9365-59e3-b93d-e0a1ff845f7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5} \\right)}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676745} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1d75d6-22d2-5ab9-b453-12fcf4cf7865" :answ