ield/id #uuid "25bb5d92-55da-5bcb-b75a-f826a1e44b57" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678789}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8143c84-2a00-5282-9ca3-f2bfa106b4d0" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=2 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{4 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=1$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{4 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10652b96-1c98-5d6a-b88e-5615c48f9f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679906} {:answer/id #uuid "27dcbd12-e676-5752-9e1b-97852310195b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679916} {:answer/id #uuid "2a34f19d-e1e0-5037-b8b6-8b91237539bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679920} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6e7476-7343-5864-a233-ad2f35780322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{2 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679977} {:answer/id #uuid "c32d8665-4c48-545b-aaa4-e8bfca5a1657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\lef